---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs14.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 25"
    link="/germany/drs/drs25"
    linkText="View DRS 25"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 14 elaborated foreign currency translation mechanics, most centrally the translation of a foreign subsidiary's own financial statements into the group's reporting currency for consolidation purposes — a genuinely important topic for any German group with foreign operations, supplementing HGB's own general currency translation provisions (§256a, established in the earlier HGB poster series).</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn — replaced by a dedicated, current group-accounts standard</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn — replaced by a dedicated, current group-accounts standard</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 14 was withdrawn and replaced by DRS 25 "Währungsumrechnung im Konzernabschluss," adopted by the HGB-Fachausschuss on 8 February 2018 and announced in the Bundesanzeiger on 3 May 2018, first applicable to fiscal years beginning after 31 December 2018. DRS 25 explicitly confirms the "modified closing rate method" under §308a HGB (in conjunction with §310(2) for jointly-managed enterprises) as the governing translation approach for subsidiaries and joint ventures — a genuinely useful confirmation of exactly HOW the statutory translation mechanic applies to consolidated foreign operations.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Foreign currency translation, including consolidation of foreign subsidiaries</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 25 — Währungsumrechnung im Konzernabschluss</strong></span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>DRS 25 adopted / announced</span><span>08.02.2018 / 03.05.2018</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>DRS 25 first applicable</span><span>Fiscal years beginning after 31.12.2018</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
